---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={`Events · ${SITE_TITLE}`} description="Upcoming events from the Optimist Club of Mount Horeb, Wisconsin." />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>

<!-- Page header -->
<section class="bg-white pt-16 pb-8">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 text-center">
    <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-optimist-blue">What's coming up</h1>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Event 1: Frolic raffle — photo right, text left -->
<section class="bg-white">
  <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 py-16">
    <div class="md:grid md:grid-cols-2 md:gap-12 md:items-center">
      <div class="md:order-2">
        <img src="/images/events/frolic-raffle.webp" alt="Drawing a winning ticket at the Summer Frolic raffle" class="w-full h-auto rounded-sm" />
      </div>
      <div class="mt-8 md:mt-0 md:order-1">
        <p class="text-sm tracking-[0.3em] uppercase text-optimist-slate">Drawing Sunday, June 14</p>
        <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-optimist-blue">Summer Frolic raffle</h2>
        <div class="mt-6 space-y-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-optimist-blue">
          <p>Twenty dollars buys a ticket. The grand prize is ten thousand. There are fifteen cash prizes in all, and the drawing happens at 5:30 in the afternoon on Sunday, June 14, in the beer tent at Grundahl Park. You don't need to be there to win.</p>
  <p>Here's the part we want you to hear. The Frolic and the Optimists are teammates. The Frolic has been very generous to us over the years, and the proceeds from this raffle come right back to the local nonprofits and youth sports clubs that work the festival every June &mdash; us included.</p>
  <p>Tickets are at Miller &amp; Sons Supermarket and the Mount Horeb Area Chamber of Commerce, or from any of us &mdash; flag down an Optimist and we'll happily sell you one.</p>
  <p>It's a good ticket to buy.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Event 2: Kid's Zone — temporary feature; pull after July 3 -->
<section class="bg-optimist-beige">
  <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 py-16">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-6">
      <figure>
        <img src="/images/events/2025-kids-zone-collage.jpg" alt="A collage from last year's Kid's Zone" class="w-full h-auto rounded-sm" />
      </figure>
      <figure>
        <img src="/images/events/2025-kids-zone-bouncy-house.jpg" alt="The bouncy house at last year's Kid's Zone" class="w-full h-auto rounded-sm" />
      </figure>
      <figure>
        <img src="/images/events/2025-kids-zone-crafts.jpg" alt="A patriotic craft project at last year's Kid's Zone" class="w-full h-auto rounded-sm" />
      </figure>
      <figure>
        <img src="/images/events/2025-kids-zone-face-painting.jpg" alt="Face painting at last year's Kid's Zone" class="w-full h-auto rounded-sm" />
      </figure>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-12 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <p class="text-sm tracking-[0.3em] uppercase text-optimist-slate">Friday, July 3</p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-optimist-blue">Kid's Zone at the Norsk July 3rd Celebration</h2>
      <div class="mt-6 space-y-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-optimist-blue">
        <p>Every July 3rd, the village gathers for the Norsk Celebration &mdash; picnic blankets, food, music, and the wait for fireworks. There's a stretch in there, especially with little kids, where the wait is the hard part. The club started the Kid's Zone a few years ago to fill it. A free station with crafts, yard games, face painting, and a bouncy house, set up on the festival grounds.</p>
        <p>The first year served twenty to forty kids. Last year it was 200+. Three patriotic craft projects, three yard games, more than ten face painting stations &mdash; all of it free thanks to club fundraising.</p>
        <p>Bring the kids. Look for the Kid's Zone tent on the afternoon and evening of July 3.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>